{
  "_doc": "Canonical cross-binding parity fixture (the NO-DRIFT guard). One file, run through every face (Rust core, Go-via-wasm, Python, TS). Each case names an op and its input envelope; every face must produce a byte-identical ok-JSON payload and an identical ok/err classification. A divergence is a CRITICAL drift bug. Inputs use the wire shape every binding shares: input_schema, default_presence, snake_case enum tags, {\"pin\":..}/{\"constrain\":{\"enum\":..}} arg policies. See SPEC.md and CLAUDE.md 'Binding parity & docs - NO DRIFT'.",
  "upstream": [
    {
      "name": "search",
      "description": "Search.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "artifact": { "type": "string" },
          "query": { "type": "string" },
          "limit": { "type": "integer" }
        },
        "required": ["artifact", "query"]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "write_file",
      "description": "Write.",
      "input_schema": { "type": "object", "properties": {} }
    }
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "project_sealed_keep_pin",
      "op": "project",
      "expect": "ok",
      "policy": {
        "default_presence": "drop",
        "tools": {
          "search": { "presence": "keep", "args": { "artifact": { "pin": "hylla" } } }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "project_passthrough_all",
      "op": "project",
      "expect": "ok",
      "policy": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": {} }
    },
    {
      "name": "project_rename_describe_constrain",
      "op": "project",
      "expect": "ok",
      "policy": {
        "default_presence": "drop",
        "tools": {
          "search": {
            "presence": "keep",
            "rename": "find",
            "description": { "override": "App find." },
            "args": {
              "artifact": { "pin": "hylla" },
              "query": { "constrain": { "enum": ["a", "b"] } },
              "limit": { "constrain": { "range": { "min": 1.0, "max": 50.0 } } }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "project_default_arg_stays_visible",
      "op": "project",
      "expect": "ok",
      "policy": {
        "default_presence": "keep",
        "tools": {
          "search": { "args": { "limit": { "default": 10 } } }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "rewrite_inject_pin_ok",
      "op": "rewrite",
      "expect": "ok",
      "call": { "name": "search", "arguments": { "query": "a", "limit": 5 } },
      "policy": {
        "tools": {
          "search": {
            "args": {
              "artifact": { "pin": "hylla" },
              "query": { "constrain": { "enum": ["a", "b"] } }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "rewrite_supplies_default_ok",
      "op": "rewrite",
      "expect": "ok",
      "call": { "name": "search", "arguments": { "artifact": "x", "query": "a" } },
      "policy": {
        "tools": { "search": { "args": { "limit": { "default": 10 } } } }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "rewrite_out_of_enum_rejects",
      "op": "rewrite",
      "expect": "err",
      "call": { "name": "search", "arguments": { "query": "z" } },
      "policy": {
        "tools": {
          "search": {
            "args": {
              "artifact": { "pin": "hylla" },
              "query": { "constrain": { "enum": ["a", "b"] } }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "rewrite_out_of_range_rejects",
      "op": "rewrite",
      "expect": "err",
      "call": { "name": "search", "arguments": { "artifact": "x", "query": "a", "limit": 999 } },
      "policy": {
        "tools": {
          "search": { "args": { "limit": { "constrain": { "range": { "min": 1.0, "max": 50.0 } } } } }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "merge_narrow_ok",
      "op": "merge",
      "expect": "ok",
      "base": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep" } } },
      "overlay": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": { "search": { "presence": "drop" } } }
    },
    {
      "name": "merge_widen_rejects",
      "op": "merge",
      "expect": "err",
      "base": { "default_presence": "drop" },
      "overlay": { "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep" } } }
    },
    {
      "_note": "Rename over an UNBOUND base name: admitted, and the ok-payload comparison is what pins the rename into every face's merged policy. This case is also the only one here that can catch a STALE go/internal/wasmbin/lagom.wasm, because a pre-88cb040 blob classifies it err while the rust reference says ok (a status drift). Err cases cannot: the comparator compares only classification for err (parity/runners/compare/main.rs).",
      "name": "merge_rename_overlay_admitted",
      "op": "merge",
      "expect": "ok",
      "base": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": {} },
      "overlay": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": { "search": { "rename": "find" } } }
    },
    {
      "_note": "The sealing half: a base that already SET a rename is a bound, so redirecting it elsewhere is rejected by every face. Classification-only (see above), so this case guards cross-face agreement on the seal; it does not detect a stale blob.",
      "name": "merge_rename_redirect_rejects",
      "op": "merge",
      "expect": "err",
      "base": {
        "default_presence": "keep",
        "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep", "rename": "find" } }
      },
      "overlay": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": { "search": { "rename": "admin" } } }
    },
    {
      "name": "validate_clean_ok",
      "op": "validate",
      "expect": "ok",
      "policy": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "artifact": { "pin": "x" } } } } }
    },
    {
      "name": "validate_drift_rejects",
      "op": "validate",
      "expect": "err",
      "policy": { "tools": { "ghost": { "args": { "x": { "pin": 1 } } } } }
    },
    {
      "name": "mint_narrow_ok",
      "op": "mint",
      "expect": "ok",
      "run_id": "agent-7",
      "base": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep" } } },
      "dynamic": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": { "search": { "presence": "drop" } } },
      "upstream_command": { "command": "srv", "args": ["-y"], "env": [] }
    },
    {
      "name": "mint_no_overlay_ok",
      "op": "mint",
      "expect": "ok",
      "run_id": "agent-8",
      "base": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep" } } },
      "dynamic": null,
      "upstream_command": { "command": "srv", "args": [], "env": [] }
    },
    {
      "name": "mint_widen_rejects",
      "op": "mint",
      "expect": "err",
      "run_id": "r",
      "base": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": { "search": { "presence": "drop" } } },
      "dynamic": { "default_presence": "keep", "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep" } } },
      "upstream_command": { "command": "srv", "args": [], "env": [] }
    },
    {
      "name": "refire_reproduces_resolved",
      "op": "refire",
      "expect": "ok",
      "mint_of": "mint_narrow_ok"
    },
    {
      "_note": "UNKNOWN-KEY BLOCK (4 cases). Every case here carries a key the Policy model does not define. A face whose engine denies unknown fields classifies err; a face whose engine ignores them classifies ok on a policy that no longer means what its author wrote. So this block is also the WASM-STALENESS GATE the fixture set previously lacked: a stale go/internal/wasmbin/lagom.wasm classifies all four ok against the rust reference's err and the comparator reports a status drift. Each case is shaped so the stale engine's op actually SUCCEEDS -- an unknown key that merely produced a different err would be invisible, because the comparator compares only classification for err (parity/runners/compare/main.rs). THIS CASE: the lagom.toml spelling `default-presence` pasted into a wire policy. On an engine that ignores it the seal reverts to the Keep default and write_file survives projection -- a sealed sandbox downgraded to passthrough, with an ok.",
      "name": "project_kebab_default_presence_rejects",
      "op": "project",
      "expect": "err",
      "policy": {
        "default-presence": "drop",
        "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep" } }
      }
    },
    {
      "_note": "Singular `arg`. On an engine that ignores it the pin vanishes: `artifact` stays in the projected schema and the agent keeps setting it itself, while the projection still reads correct under audit.",
      "name": "project_typoed_args_key_rejects",
      "op": "project",
      "expect": "err",
      "policy": {
        "default_presence": "drop",
        "tools": {
          "search": {
            "presence": "keep",
            "arg": { "artifact": { "pin": "hylla" } }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_note": "Misspelled `presence`. On an engine that ignores it the tool falls through to default_presence and is dropped -- the opposite of the author's intent, with no diagnostic.",
      "name": "project_typoed_presence_key_rejects",
      "op": "project",
      "expect": "err",
      "policy": {
        "default_presence": "drop",
        "tools": { "search": { "presense": "keep" } }
      }
    },
    {
      "_note": "`maximum` inside a range. On an engine that ignores it the bound parses as {min:1,max:none} -- a PARTIAL parse -- so limit=999 is admitted by a policy whose author capped it at 50. Half the bound enforced, and the call reads legitimate.",
      "name": "rewrite_range_typoed_maximum_rejects",
      "op": "rewrite",
      "expect": "err",
      "call": { "name": "search", "arguments": { "artifact": "x", "query": "a", "limit": 999 } },
      "policy": {
        "tools": {
          "search": {
            "args": { "limit": { "constrain": { "range": { "min": 1.0, "maximum": 50.0 } } } }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_note": "MINT-SHAPE half of the unknown-key block. The four cases above bound `Policy` only; this one bounds the persisted mint shapes (MintRecord -> PolicySources -> UpstreamCommand), which no other case reaches. A refire case carrying `record` hands that on-disk shape across the same JSON boundary in every face, so the guard is compared rather than bypassed -- unlike `upstream_command`, which the Python and Node runners destructure into command/args/env and never pass whole. THIS CASE: singular `arg` in both recorded upstream commands. On an engine that ignores it `args` falls to its `#[serde(default)]` empty vec, refire returns ok, and the proxy launches the correct executable stripped of `--sealed` -- what RUNS changes, and the record still reads correct under audit. Everything else in the record is well-formed, so the err is attributable to the unknown key alone.",
      "name": "refire_record_typoed_args_key_rejects",
      "op": "refire",
      "expect": "err",
      "record": {
        "run_id": "agent-9",
        "sources": {
          "config_paths": [],
          "upstream": { "command": "srv", "arg": ["--sealed"], "env": [] },
          "dynamic_inputs": null
        },
        "resolved": {
          "policy": {
            "default_presence": "drop",
            "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep" } }
          },
          "upstream": { "command": "srv", "arg": ["--sealed"], "env": [] }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_note": "DISCRIMINATION CONTROL for the case above: the same record with the key spelled `args`. Every face must classify it ok, so the sibling's err is attributable to the unknown key and not to some unrelated defect in the record's shape. Its ok-payload is also byte-compared, so this case doubles as a staleness detector on the refire path.",
      "name": "refire_record_inline_ok",
      "op": "refire",
      "expect": "ok",
      "record": {
        "run_id": "agent-9",
        "sources": {
          "config_paths": [],
          "upstream": { "command": "srv", "args": ["--sealed"], "env": [] },
          "dynamic_inputs": null
        },
        "resolved": {
          "policy": {
            "default_presence": "drop",
            "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep" } }
          },
          "upstream": { "command": "srv", "args": ["--sealed"], "env": [] }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_note": "Forbid on a declared argument removes it from the schema and names it in the addendum; forbid on an undeclared one changes nothing visible.",
      "name": "project_forbid_declared_and_undeclared",
      "op": "project",
      "expect": "ok",
      "policy": {
        "default_presence": "drop",
        "tools": {
          "search": { "presence": "keep", "args": { "limit": "forbid", "version_pin": "forbid" } }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "rewrite_forbid_refuses_a_carrying_call",
      "op": "rewrite",
      "expect": "err",
      "call": { "name": "search", "arguments": { "artifact": "x", "query": "a", "version_pin": 3 } },
      "policy": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "version_pin": "forbid" } } } }
    },
    {
      "_note": "DISCRIMINATION CONTROL for the case above: the same call without the forbidden argument is forwarded unchanged.",
      "name": "rewrite_forbid_absent_is_forwarded",
      "op": "rewrite",
      "expect": "ok",
      "call": { "name": "search", "arguments": { "artifact": "x", "query": "a" } },
      "policy": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "version_pin": "forbid" } } } }
    },
    {
      "name": "merge_constrain_to_forbid_narrows",
      "op": "merge",
      "expect": "ok",
      "base": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "limit": { "constrain": { "range": { "max": 5.0 } } } } } } },
      "overlay": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "limit": "forbid" } } } }
    },
    {
      "name": "merge_forbid_to_passthrough_widens",
      "op": "merge",
      "expect": "err",
      "base": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "limit": "forbid" } } } },
      "overlay": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "limit": "passthrough" } } } }
    },
    {
      "name": "merge_pin_to_forbid_widens",
      "op": "merge",
      "expect": "err",
      "base": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "artifact": { "pin": "hylla" } } } } },
      "overlay": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "artifact": "forbid" } } } }
    },
    {
      "name": "validate_forbid_on_an_undeclared_arg_is_grounded",
      "op": "validate",
      "expect": "ok",
      "policy": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "version_pin": "forbid" } } } }
    },
    {
      "name": "validate_forbid_on_a_required_arg_is_drift",
      "op": "validate",
      "expect": "err",
      "policy": { "tools": { "search": { "args": { "artifact": "forbid" } } } }
    },
    {
      "name": "mint_forbid_overlay_narrows",
      "op": "mint",
      "expect": "ok",
      "run_id": "agent-f",
      "base": { "default_presence": "drop", "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep" } } },
      "dynamic": { "default_presence": "drop", "tools": { "search": { "args": { "version_pin": "forbid" } } } },
      "upstream_command": { "command": "srv", "args": [], "env": [] }
    },
    {
      "name": "policy_to_document_every_rule",
      "op": "policy_to_document",
      "expect": "ok",
      "policy": {
        "default_presence": "drop",
        "tools": {
          "search": {
            "presence": "keep",
            "rename": "find",
            "description": { "override": "Find." },
            "args": {
              "artifact": { "pin": "hylla" },
              "query": { "constrain": { "pattern": "^a" } },
              "limit": { "default": 10 },
              "version_pin": "forbid"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "policy_from_document_ok",
      "op": "policy_from_document",
      "expect": "ok",
      "document": {
        "lagom_policy": 1,
        "default_presence": "drop",
        "tools": { "search": { "presence": "keep", "args": { "version_pin": "forbid" } } }
      }
    },
    {
      "_note": "A stored ceiling that lost default_presence must be refused; the bare Policy shape would read it as keep (passthrough).",
      "name": "policy_from_document_missing_presence_refused",
      "op": "policy_from_document",
      "expect": "err",
      "document": { "lagom_policy": 1, "tools": {} }
    },
    {
      "name": "policy_from_document_future_format_refused",
      "op": "policy_from_document",
      "expect": "err",
      "document": { "lagom_policy": 2, "default_presence": "drop" }
    },
    {
      "name": "policy_from_document_missing_format_refused",
      "op": "policy_from_document",
      "expect": "err",
      "document": { "default_presence": "drop" }
    },
    {
      "_note": "Control for the *_text cases below: verbatim text with no repeat reads like the object form.",
      "name": "policy_from_document_text_ok",
      "op": "policy_from_document",
      "expect": "ok",
      "document_text": "{\"lagom_policy\":1,\"default_presence\":\"drop\",\"tools\":{\"search\":{\"presence\":\"keep\",\"args\":{\"version_pin\":\"forbid\"}}}}"
    },
    {
      "_note": "A repeated key must be refused at every level; a last-wins read would unseal or drop the forbid. Carried as text because a JSON loader merges repeats.",
      "name": "policy_from_document_repeated_default_presence_refused",
      "op": "policy_from_document",
      "expect": "err",
      "document_text": "{\"lagom_policy\":1,\"default_presence\":\"drop\",\"default_presence\":\"keep\"}"
    },
    {
      "name": "policy_from_document_repeated_format_refused",
      "op": "policy_from_document",
      "expect": "err",
      "document_text": "{\"lagom_policy\":2,\"lagom_policy\":1,\"default_presence\":\"drop\"}"
    },
    {
      "name": "policy_from_document_repeated_tool_refused",
      "op": "policy_from_document",
      "expect": "err",
      "document_text": "{\"lagom_policy\":1,\"default_presence\":\"keep\",\"tools\":{\"s\":{\"presence\":\"drop\"},\"s\":{\"presence\":\"keep\"}}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "policy_from_document_repeated_presence_refused",
      "op": "policy_from_document",
      "expect": "err",
      "document_text": "{\"lagom_policy\":1,\"default_presence\":\"keep\",\"tools\":{\"s\":{\"presence\":\"drop\",\"presence\":\"keep\"}}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "policy_from_document_repeated_arg_refused",
      "op": "policy_from_document",
      "expect": "err",
      "document_text": "{\"lagom_policy\":1,\"default_presence\":\"keep\",\"tools\":{\"s\":{\"args\":{\"v\":\"forbid\",\"v\":\"passthrough\"}}}}"
    },
    {
      "_note": "A bare policy defaults a missing default_presence to keep; storing it must refuse rather than write an assumed keep.",
      "name": "policy_to_document_missing_presence_refused",
      "op": "policy_to_document",
      "expect": "err",
      "policy": { "tools": {} }
    },
    {
      "name": "policy_to_document_repeated_key_refused",
      "op": "policy_to_document",
      "expect": "err",
      "policy_text": "{\"default_presence\":\"drop\",\"tools\":{\"s\":{\"args\":{\"v\":\"forbid\",\"v\":\"passthrough\"}}}}"
    }
  ]
}
